translate: compare a cached translate's key over the elements in use, as it
is hashed. translate_cache_find hashed the key's elements in use but
compared the whole struct translate_key with memcmp: 920 bytes on the 68k
(38 elements of 24 bytes), all of them on every hit. With 0011, u_vbuf
translates every draw on a big-endian virgl, so AssaultCube looked up the
cache once or twice a draw, and GCC's inline byte loop for that memcmp was
the hottest guest block: 4.5 to 5% of the emulation thread (Team 5, W156's
and W159b's profiles, 27 and 28 October 2026). A key's elements past
nr_elements are unused, and nr_elements itself is compared.
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/translate/translate_cache.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/translate/translate_cache.c
@@ -91,10 +91,13 @@
                                         struct translate_key *key)
 {
    unsigned hash_key = create_key(key);
+   /* Compare the part of the key the hash covers (its elements in use), not
+    * the whole of it with every unused element: that was 920 bytes a lookup,
+    * one or two lookups a draw when u_vbuf translates every draw. */
    struct translate *translate = (struct translate*)
       cso_hash_find_data_from_template(&cache->hash,
                                        hash_key,
-                                       key, sizeof(*key));
+                                       key, translate_hash_key_size(key));
 
    if (!translate) {
       /* create/insert */
